  "kind": "recipe",
  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "standard",
    "description": "r0b0tlab's native Atlas runtime (Avarok-Cybersecurity's Rust/CUDA `spark` engine, AGPL-3.0-only, not vLLM or SGLang) for NVIDIA Nemotron 3.5 Lightning 30B-A3B NVFP4 with NVIDIA's official DSpark draft head on one Spark, from r0b0tlab/nemotron-3.5-lightning-atlas-sm121 at 4ecde533 (MIT; Atlas source 3f929293, binary sha256:1111f86b). UPSTREAM STATUS: 'public reproducibility WIP / not qualified' - the native source, build and runtime gates and the immutable image are complete, but the full r0b0bench core-subset run is not (the BFCL multi-turn lane stalled at 129/200 rows and is kept as diagnostic), so upstream makes no full-suite quality or throughput claim. Runs upstream's immutable image unchanged with its launch_serve.sh settings: DSpark gamma 4 (scheduler K=3) with a 1,024-token window, FP8 target KV with high-precision attention boundaries, BF16 drafter KV, 50,016-token context, batch 8, prefill 8,192, memory utilisation 0.75 (upstream warns not to serve DSpark at 0.85), the slai scheduling policy, qwen3_coder tool parser and thinking off by default. Upstream's selected-lane WIP numbers (not claims, not measured here): C1 84.18 tok/s and 152.84 / 168.42 / 155.84 aggregate at C2 / C4 / C6, GSM8K 191/200. The option switches to upstream's autoregressive profile; its 1M-token AR profile (batch 1, 3000 s request timeout) is not offered. Target checkpoint e8f3c7c4 is the revision r0b0tlab's sibling Nemotron repositories name; upstream provides weights locally. Physical Spark acceptance is pending.",
